# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the React + Vite project following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version automatically resolved by npm)
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies (183 packages added)

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified: `src/App.jsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react"`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the App component, positioned right after the existing `<Analytics />` component
- This placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all routes and page navigations

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for React applications:
- Retrieved latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Used the React-specific integration path (`@vercel/speed-insights/react`)
- Placed the component at the root level of the application for complete coverage
- Maintained consistency with the existing Vercel Analytics setup

## Verification

✅ **Build Test**: Successfully built the project with `npm run build`
- Build completed without errors in 2.65s
- All assets compiled correctly

✅ **Linter Test**: Ran `npm run lint`
- No new linting errors introduced by the changes
- Pre-existing linting errors in other files (ProjectGallery.jsx, ProjectsPage.jsx) remain unchanged

## Next Steps

To enable Speed Insights data collection:
1. Deploy the project to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. View performance metrics after deployment and user visits

